# Per-device topic access.
#
# Signaling topics are signaling/<node_id>/<message type>. A device must be able
# to publish to its peers' topics and subscribe to its own. Mosquitto has no way
# to bind a topic to a device's node_id, so the practical split is: everyone may
# publish, nobody may subscribe outside their own subtree.
#
# Add one block per device account, using the node_id shown on its
# "My Device" card in Settings > Sync.

# Publishing to a peer is how pairing works at all, so it cannot be restricted
# to known peers up front. A forged message is useless: it will not carry a
# valid signature.
pattern write signaling/+/+

# Reading is the part that matters. Replace the username and node_id per device.
# user laptop
# topic read signaling/<laptop-node-id>/+

# user phone
# topic read signaling/<phone-node-id>/+
